{
  "default": true,
  "locale": "en",
  "scene": "scn_rgudy7nl",
  "schema": "patter/strings@0",
  "strings": {
    "C_3xyl25ub": "Sit in silence for a while",
    "C_5y4fmqoe": "You're going home, after a long time away",
    "C_7o7v5dyf": "Tell him why you're crossing",
    "C_avxwmcp0": "Ask about the river",
    "C_cfobbptu": "Look back the way you came",
    "C_djbk4f9k": "Look for the far bank",
    "C_hpgznd2n": "Ask about him",
    "C_htpvtu2b": "Say it's nobody's business",
    "C_m5hfa5ti": "You're leaving, and you won't be back",
    "C_sdy3i5y6": "Ask how long he has rowed this crossing",
    "L_2yr65uio": "Me? Not much to tell. I had a wife who liked the far bank better than this one. I row over most nights, and I row back most mornings.",
    "L_7q871vga": "Fog's coming in. It always does, round about now.",
    "L_a6bwx2xe": "Forty-one years in March. Thirty of them in this boat. She was my father's before she was mine, and she'll be nobody's after.",
    "L_d656xmon": "My father used to sing out here. I never picked it up.",
    "L_djv7yus4": "Home. It'll have gone on without you. They always do. Doesn't mean there's no room.",
    "L_dpswdpq3": "There. Now it's done.",
    "L_eiy2zzmk": "Then look back once, from the middle. Everyone should, once.",
    "L_hsaygfo0": "Fair. The river doesn't ask either.",
    "L_rmsqiq2n": "Deeper than it looks and colder than you'd think. People drop things over the side and swear they never hear them land.",
    "L_t10n62qy": "Don't fret about the coins. The river's in no hurry, and neither am I.",
    "T_0xbabs79": "An owl calls from the far side, once, and does not call again.",
    "T_6r9kg1de": "He leans on the oar and the jetty slides away. Within a dozen strokes the lamp is a smudge, then it is gone, and there is only the water and the creak of the rowlock.",
    "T_866scqn1": "He says it lightly, the way people say heavy things.",
    "T_jp39lpe0": "You turn on the bench and peer ahead. The fog has closed in, soft and total.",
    "T_knljstb6": "You turn and look back. There is nothing to see: no lamp, no jetty, only the fog closing in behind the boat like a door.",
    "T_lt6lsktr": "The oar dips, rises, drips. Dips, rises, drips.",
    "T_q9o7flul": "You listen. Nothing lands.",
  },
}
